    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Massa</span></b> , ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> L. Terentius Massa,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				31, 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">40,
			35</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Baebius Massa, <i>a notorious informer and
			sycophant</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 3, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 1,
			35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>The name of a slave</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Petr. 69</span></i>.</div>
